"},{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"unconnected_items: []"}],"reasoning":"I verified the thermal spokes exist in the saved filled_polygon and DRC reports zero unconnected items, so the net is connected as saved and this is not a defect. It is recorded as an info-level concern because GND continuity rests on a single via plus a fill state that the toolchain is forbidden from regenerating; for a disposable review fixture this is acceptable, but it is the one connection not corroborated by any explicit track."},{"id":"geometry-probe-assert-noise","title":"Geometry probe console contains repeated internal KiCad assertion failures","location":"work/geometry/console.log","condition":"The geometry probe run emitted three instances of 'assert \"m_choices.GetCount() > 0\" failed in PROPERTY_ENUM(): No enum choices defined' from pcbnew internals alongside its normal output.","mechanism":"Non-fatal assertion failures inside the measuring tool raise the possibility of partially initialized tool state producing unreliable measurements, even though the process exited 0.","severity":"info","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"work/geometry/console.log","locator":"lines 2-4 (PROPERTY_ENUM assert messages)"},{"path":"work/geometry/geometry.json","locator":"tracks[] five segment entries each width_mm 0.25; counts 3 footprints / 6 track items / 1 zone"},{"path":"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb","locator":"five (segment ... (width 0.25)) entries, one (via ...), one (zone ...)"}],"reasoning":"I cross-checked every number the probe reported (segment count, widths, pad positions, via, zone) against the raw native board file and they all match, so the measurement outcome is trustworthy and the geometry pass verdict stands. The assertion spam is tool noise worth flagging so the operator knows the probe's environment is slightly degraded, not a defect in the candidate."}]},"ttft_ms":75601,"type":"result","duration_ms":121224,"uuid":"d1dcd293-74e8-4c90-995b-b80373a9eea3","ttft